    {
      "input": "*He asks Niles Vanner who they think he is and where he comes from.*",
      "outcome": "success",
      "exception": null,
      "narration": "Niles Vanner's fingers still the empty pan of his scale, his expression settling into something patient and appraising. \"Who you are and where you're from,\" he says, tone even and unhurried, \"is what you choose to tell me, or choose not to. I don't keep a registry here, and I don't ask for papers.\" His eyes, aging faster than the rest of him, move over Nicco plainly—tall, heavy, the faint early march of white. \"You look like a man who's been walking. Beyond that, I don't guess. Guessing wrong costs more than not knowing.\"",
